# Spanish changes what it is handed. b, d and g between vowels are said as
# the approximants B, D and G; two consonants alike are said as one; and a
# nasal at the end of a word takes the place of the consonant that begins the
# next. That is Spanish, and a module that is to say another language's
# phones has to say them as they were given.
#
# Measured, with engine/accent/chassis.py in OpenEvv-sapi5 (github.com/joshknnd1982/OpenEvv-sapi5): with these in place of IBM's, b d
# g stay stops wherever they stand and a doubled consonant is two.
rule lenition takes 3 from st_phnol.obj
  afresh
  call ZZfence_null
  match
end

rule no_span_double_phone takes 3 from st_phnol.obj
  afresh
  call ZZfence_null
  match
end

rule syneresis takes 3 from st_phnol.obj
  afresh
  call ZZfence_null
  match
end

rule span_phrase_level_rules takes 3 from st_phnol.obj
  afresh
  call ZZfence_null
  match
end
